From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 11:59:22 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] calcActiveVoices_internal: keep protected voices active

PROTECTED was only consulted when choosing a voice slot to steal. The
active-voice ranking sorted purely by volume, so a quiet protected voice
(typically music) was made inactive despite the documented contract
"Protected voices are always played". Protected candidates now join the
must-live group ahead of the volume sort.

Fixes upstream #298.
---
 src/core/soloud.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/core/soloud.cpp b/src/core/soloud.cpp
index 872c264..d53ab70 100644
--- a/src/core/soloud.cpp
+++ b/src/core/soloud.cpp
@@ -1981,7 +1981,9 @@ namespace SoLoud
 			{
 				mActiveVoice[candidates] = i;
 				candidates++;
-				if (mVoice[i]->mFlags & AudioSourceInstance::INAUDIBLE_TICK)
+				// Ticking and protected voices are kept ahead of the volume sort;
+				// protected voices are documented as always played.
+				if (mVoice[i]->mFlags & (AudioSourceInstance::INAUDIBLE_TICK | AudioSourceInstance::PROTECTED))
 				{
 					mActiveVoice[candidates - 1] = mActiveVoice[mustlive];
 					mActiveVoice[mustlive] = i;
